// How everything flowssss
USER REGISTERS
─────────────
React → POST /api/auth/register
  → MongoDB saves user (password hashed)
  → publishEvent('user.registered', { email, username })  ← fire & forget
  → Returns 201 immediately  ← user doesn't wait for email

  [Background — Kafka Consumer]
  → Picks up 'user.registered' event
  → Nodemailer sends welcome email to user's Gmail


USER LOGS IN
────────────
React → POST /api/auth/login
  → Verifies password with bcrypt
  → Creates access token (15 min) + refresh token (7 days)
  → publishEvent('user.loggedin', { email, username, timestamp })
  → Returns tokens immediately

  [Background — Kafka Consumer]
  → Picks up 'user.loggedin' event
  → Nodemailer sends login alert email


USER TYPES "London" IN SEARCH BOX
──────────────────────────────────
L → debounce timer resets
Lo → debounce timer resets
Lon → debounce timer resets
Lond → debounce timer resets
Londo → debounce timer resets
London → [500ms of silence] → fires ONE API call ✓


EVERY DAY AT 8AM (Cron)
────────────────────────
→ Finds all users with savedCity + digestEnabled
→ Fetches fresh weather from OpenWeatherMap for each
→ publishEvent('weather.digest', { email, city, weatherData })
→ Kafka consumer sends personalized weather email to each user


EVERY MIDNIGHT (Cron)
──────────────────────
→ Scans all users' refreshTokens arrays in MongoDB
→ Verifies each token — removes expired ones
→ Keeps DB clean


EVERY 9 MINUTES (Cron)
───────────────────────
→ Pre-fetches Delhi, Mumbai, London, New York, Tokyo, Paris
→ Stores each in Redis (10 min TTL)
→ Users searching these cities always get instant cache hits


------------------Docker ,K8, AWS----------------------
Without Docker, you say "it works on my machine" — Docker makes it work EVERYWHERE the same way.
Without Kubernetes, if your app crashes at 3AM, nobody restarts it. K8s does that automatically.
Without AWS, your app dies when you close your laptop. AWS keeps it running 24/7.The full roadmapPhase 1 — Docker
  └── Containerize backend, frontend, MongoDB, Redis, Kafka
  └── Wire them together with docker-compose (local)

Phase 2 — Kubernetes  
  └── Write K8s configs (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets)
  └── Test locally with minikube

Phase 3 — AWS
  └── Push images to ECR (AWS's Docker Hub)
  └── Create EKS cluster (AWS's managed Kubernetes)
  └── Deploy everything to the cloud

  
  Your laptop (Windows)
  └── Docker Container
        ├── Ubuntu Linux (inside the container)
        ├── Node.js 20
        ├── Your backend code
        └── All npm packages

AWS Server (also Linux)
  └── Same Docker Container  ← identical, guaranteed